     1	//! Client-side object storage gateway.
     2	//!
     3	//! This module is the synchronous facade that the rest of the codebase uses to read,
     4	//! write, and search Git objects. It hides three orthogonal concerns:
     5	//!
     6	//! 1. **Storage backend selection** — local-only, or local cache plus a remote
     7	//!    object_store-backed bucket (S3/R2). Backend is chosen at construction time from
     8	//!    `LIBRA_STORAGE_*` environment variables and `vault.env.*` config entries.
     9	//! 2. **Sync/async bridging** — most of the codebase is synchronous CLI logic, while
    10	//!    every storage backend is async. A dedicated multi-thread Tokio runtime owned by
    11	//!    this module runs the async work and the CLI thread blocks on a `mpsc::channel`,
    12	//!    avoiding nested-runtime panics that would occur if we drove the storage from the
    13	//!    main runtime.
    14	//! 3. **Background object indexing** — every successful `put` enqueues an index-update
    15	//!    message for the cloud-backup object index. The consumer runs serially on the
    16	//!    background runtime so concurrent writers cannot deadlock on the SQLite database.
    17	//!
    18	//! Search supports Git's revision navigation suffixes (`HEAD`, `~`, `^`).
    19	
